WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.750
Usually, it's not too tough to guess how a
film is going to turn out, especially in the

00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:09.651
days of multiple trailers, trailers for different
regions, teasers for those trailers, and even

00:00:09.651 --> 00:00:11.440
sometimes teasers for the teasers.

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:15.980
Other times... it's not quite as easy, as
these films with surprising Rotten Tomatoes

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:16.980
scores prove.

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:19.840
Mortal Engines should have been a surefire
hit.

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:24.560
It's got Peter Jackson as a co-producer and
co-writer, and it's based on a successful

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:25.560
YA franchise.

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:29.360
Heck, it's about giant, mobile cities that
eat each other to survive.

00:00:29.540 --> 00:00:34.580
Seems like a license to print money, but unfortunately
that still wasn't enough to succeed with fans

00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:35.480
and critics.

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:40.240
Earning a 26% on Rotten Tomatoes is rough
by almost any standard, but there's something

00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:44.480
odd about watching a film that seemed tailor
made to launch a massive franchise sputter

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:46.700
out before it even left the starting line.

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:49.280
The Mortal Engines didn't just bomb with critics.

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:55.420
According to IMDb, the film has an estimated
budget of $100 million and as of late January

00:00:55.420 --> 00:01:00.320
2019, it had just barely cleared the $80 million
mark in worldwide gross.

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:04.300
It's doubtful we'll see a followup no matter
how ready-made for success Mortal Engines

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:05.300
seems on paper.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:10.420
The Transformers franchise isn't exactly known
as a critical darling, even if it does seem

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:12.400
to have the uncanny ability to print money.

00:01:12.620 --> 00:01:16.950
While the original live-action entry for the
Robots in Disguise earned a surprisingly respectable

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:21.920
57% on Rotten Tomatoes, subsequent entries
haven't fared as well.

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:27.330
Few would reasonably expect the first Transformers
spinoff to roar into theaters with a 93% on

00:01:27.330 --> 00:01:29.960
Rotten Tomatoes to round out 2018.

00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:34.570
Luckily, Bumblebee has got some star power
in its tank and a can't-miss formula as its

00:01:34.570 --> 00:01:35.140
chassis.

00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:40.240
Director Travis Knight injects the flick with
late '80s flavor thanks to its period setting

00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:44.450
and a Guardians of the Galaxy-like approach
to the soundtrack, picking appropriate, timely

00:01:44.450 --> 00:01:45.860
hits to keep the energy up.

00:01:46.110 --> 00:01:50.300
Meanwhile, Hailee Steinfeld's turn as the
young Charlie gives the movie more than enough

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:55.560
heart to let audiences get invested in her
friendship with the anthropomorphic VW Bug.

00:01:55.560 --> 00:01:56.940
"Hide hide!”

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:08.740
The first Mamma Mia! movie was a hit with
fans of the original Broadway musical and

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:11.009
anyone who knows the truth that ABBA rules.

00:02:11.009 --> 00:02:15.250
That didn't necessarily translate to making
it a hit with critics since it was only able

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:17.880
to attain a 55% on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:22.340
But the truly baffling decision to stage a
sequel ended up paying off both critically

00:02:22.340 --> 00:02:23.580
and financially.

00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:29.189
The fantastically titled Mamma Mia!: Here
We Go Again is certifiably fresh at 81% and

00:02:29.189 --> 00:02:32.480
raked in $394 million at the box office.

00:02:32.580 --> 00:02:36.560
While much of the enjoyment of the sequel
comes from the ridiculous setups for its musical

00:02:36.569 --> 00:02:41.489
set pieces, the true shining beacon of Here
We Go Again is Cher, who steals every scene

00:02:41.489 --> 00:02:43.980
she's in as the mother of Meryl Streep's character.

00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:48.820
The raucous Mediterranean musical celebration
is dripping with schmaltz, but it works.

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:52.260
"It's not punishment; it's the opposite.

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:54.940
It's like a gift to myself."

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:59.500
Walking the very thin line between earnest
and cheesy makes for some magical moments

00:02:59.620 --> 00:03:02.120
in what could have been a money-grabbing,
soulless sequel.

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:06.760
Nicolas Cage doesn't seem like he can say
no to a movie, which often leads to him getting

00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:08.680
stuck in some absolute clunkers.

00:03:08.780 --> 00:03:13.900
However, his chaotic, messy turn in Mandy
arrives in service of the first film in years

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:17.340
to take full advantage of Cage at his peak
gonzo sensibilities.

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:22.940
Mandy became an instant cult hit and had critics
raving after its release, resulting in a 91%

00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:24.080
on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:28.799
Mandy follows Cage on a mind-bending, gory
journey of revenge aimed at a cult and a group

00:03:28.799 --> 00:03:30.659
of drug-addled demon bikers.

00:03:30.659 --> 00:03:34.040
It doesn't necessarily sound like a movie
that might be sitting at the top of critics'

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:39.329
lists in 2018, but fans and critics alike
responded to the stylized violence and shocking

00:03:39.329 --> 00:03:40.500
imagery of Mandy.

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:45.939
The perfect storm of Academy Award and Golden
Globe Award nominee Ava DuVernay directing

00:03:45.940 --> 00:03:50.280
an adaptation of the children's classic A
Wrinkle in Time still couldn't wow critics.

00:03:50.440 --> 00:03:55.099
The film is currently saddled with a 42% on
the service, with an even lower fan rating

00:03:55.099 --> 00:03:56.370
of 28%.

00:03:56.370 --> 00:04:00.849
A Wrinkle in Time introduces audiences to
the precocious Meg Murray, played by newcomer

00:04:00.849 --> 00:04:05.320
Storm Reid, as she's led on a time and space-bending
journey in search of her father.

00:04:05.480 --> 00:04:09.700
While some critics were wowed by the film's
CGI wonders, others felt that the effects

00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:12.560
bogged the film down and made it a little
too cheesy.

00:04:12.760 --> 00:04:15.040
"That's one word for it."

00:04:15.460 --> 00:04:19.071
The film wears its heart and ambitions on
it sleeves and it will be interesting to see

00:04:19.080 --> 00:04:20.640
if it persists as a cult favorite.

00:04:21.340 --> 00:04:25.260
2018 ended up being a banner year for Spider-Man
related media.

00:04:25.260 --> 00:04:29.640
While Venom took a bit of a beating from critics,
the film has amassed a fervent fanbase and

00:04:29.640 --> 00:04:32.690
more than made back its estimated $100 million
budget.

00:04:32.690 --> 00:04:36.760
Spider-Man: Into the Spider-Verse could have
been the animated also-ran to cap off the

00:04:36.760 --> 00:04:41.280
year, but it ended up blowing the Spider-Man
franchise wide open and impressing critics

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:42.280
at the same time.

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:46.070
It's currently sitting at 97% on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:04:46.070 --> 00:04:49.920
Spider-Verse's stellar animation alone would
set it up to be a game-changer, but the immense

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:53.910
heart at the core of the story propels it
into something truly special.

00:04:53.910 --> 00:04:58.280
Even critics exhausted by the superhero movie
bubble had to admit that Into the Spider-Verse

00:04:58.280 --> 00:04:59.280
was a step above.

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:04.500
"Wherever I go the wind follows, and the wind
smells like rain."

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:08.140
Game Night could have come and gone without
much fanfare due to its incredibly generic

00:05:08.140 --> 00:05:12.200
and bland marketing campaign, which hid a
raucous, critic-pleasing comedy.

00:05:12.370 --> 00:05:16.980
The movie stars Rachel McAdams and Jason Bateman
as a competitive couple who have bonded over

00:05:16.980 --> 00:05:18.480
their shared love of games.

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:22.340
Kyle Chandler, playing Bateman's brother,
hosts a game night framed as an immersive

00:05:22.340 --> 00:05:24.750
experience in which one of the guests is kidnapped.

00:05:24.980 --> 00:05:25.820
The twist?

00:05:25.830 --> 00:05:26.870
The kidnapping is real.

00:05:26.870 --> 00:05:28.930
"First one that follows us gets shot!”

00:05:28.930 --> 00:05:30.310
“Ok, roger that.

00:05:30.310 --> 00:05:30.960
You drive safe.”

00:05:32.760 --> 00:05:33.840
“That was amazing!”

00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:35.080
“Really good.”

00:05:36.040 --> 00:05:40.180
Adam Graham of the Detroit News gave Game
Night credit for being an adult movie that

00:05:40.180 --> 00:05:44.500
never stooped to lowbrow humor, calling it
quote, "a crowd-pleaser to which you'll want

00:05:44.500 --> 00:05:45.260
to be invited."

00:05:45.500 --> 00:05:51.160
All that positive buzz added up to Game Night
scoring an 84% overall rating on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:05:52.020 --> 00:05:56.520
Duncan Jones is an interesting director with
a Tomatometer record that was only recently

00:05:56.520 --> 00:06:01.180
derailed by his odd stint as the director
of the critically ill-fated Warcraft movie.

00:06:01.180 --> 00:06:07.000
Before that, he was riding high with the low-key
sci-fi masterpiece Moon and his 2011 follow-up,

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:09.080
the Jake Gyllenhaal thriller Source Code.

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:14.300
Warcraft was still a financial success, especially
outside the United States, but fans were eager

00:06:14.300 --> 00:06:18.090
for Jones to return to his own stories, characters
and worlds.

00:06:18.090 --> 00:06:23.500
His next piece of work, 2018's Netflix-distributed
Mute, was described as a Blade Runner-esque

00:06:23.500 --> 00:06:25.860
excursion, suggesting a strong rebound.

00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:26.920
Not quite.

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:31.880
While Mute looked like a return to form, it
ended up being a generic, lifeless mess with

00:06:31.880 --> 00:06:36.260
not much to say and not much to show for it
except a 20% on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:06:36.860 --> 00:06:40.640
What happens when a troubled biopic about
an infamous gangster that's been in production

00:06:40.650 --> 00:06:45.490
for years ends up being a dull, boring slog
anchored by a bizarre performance from John

00:06:45.490 --> 00:06:46.000
Travolta?

00:06:46.200 --> 00:06:50.240
It nets a resounding 0% overall on Rotten
tomatoes.

00:06:50.240 --> 00:06:52.960
Biopics starring famous actors are usually
critical hits.

00:06:52.960 --> 00:06:53.460
This one?

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:54.420
Not so much.

00:06:54.460 --> 00:06:58.880
Rolling Stone's Peter Travers spoke for many
of his peers when he compared it to a lifeless

00:06:58.880 --> 00:07:00.280
version of The Sopranos.

00:07:00.280 --> 00:07:01.560
"I can't watch this again."

